Z||000000||N_Man||06-13-2000||01:53 PM||||At suspension restorations they sell engine cradle mount bushings for $54.  What I need to know is are these the cradle bushings or the motor mounts?<P>Im looking for new cradle bushings and part stores tell me to call the GM dealer, who cant get all of em.  And the ones he can get are WAY over priced.    <P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||06-13-2000||03:00 PM||||That sounds like the engine or tranny mount rubber bushings.  Youir GM dealer should be able to get the front cradle mount bushings.  They cost around $11 or $12!... the same price as the Fiero Store  <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com/</A> <P>Prothane also offers the poly urethane cradle bushings <A HREF="http://www.prothane.com/Main_Menu/main_menu.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.prothane.com/Main_Menu/main_menu.html</A>    <BR>or <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com/fiero-prothane.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.suspension.com/fiero-prothane.htm</A> <P>for less than either Fiero Store or Chris West   <A HREF="http://home.earthlink.net/~chriswest/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.earthlink.net/~chriswest/index.html</A> <BR>CW also offers aluminum cradle bushings as well as urethane engine and tranny mounts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>hope this helps!<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||06-13-2000||03:24 PM||||Yes, Suspension restorations sells the cradle bushings.  They are poly-urethane.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||06-13-2000||10:41 PM||||you can get the Prothane Cradle mount set from  <A HREF="http://www.nopi.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nopi.com</A>   part #7-502-b (the B stands for the color replace with B=black R=red Y=Yellow or P=pink) for $46 including shipping... (ups ground) thats what i paid!  or call Chris or Danny at 770-434-0200 but if your really into the thrill and need the AWSOME handling get the ones from Chris West!||||reg||1
